	<h1>About</h1>
	<PageNav />

	<p>I'm a data scientist at Essentia Health. Before that, I was a political scientist.</p>

	<p>
		I have a Ph.D. in political science from the University of Minnesota, where I studied Congress
		and the American welfare state. After that I taught for a year at the University of Minnesota,
		Morris, which is also where I went to college.
	</p>

	<p>
		The <a href="/blog">blog</a> has data and analysis write-ups. The <a href="/archive">archive</a> has
		what I wrote about Congress and academic life from 2014 to 2017, left as it was.
	</p>

	<p>
		I live in Minnesota. Outside of work I cheer for midwestern sports teams, explore state parks,
		and watch PBS.
	</p>

	<p>
